---
/**
 * The text of a story. DS: Prosa (`.ct-prosa`).
 *
 * The page renders the Markdown into the slot (`<Content />`), so the whole
 * story is in the HTML from the start: no JavaScript is involved in showing
 * it, which is what search engines need (DS › Prosa, SEO brief › §8).
 *
 * All its styles are in app.css › Story components, because the elements
 * inside come from Markdown and cannot carry utility classes: chapters
 * (`<h2 id="capitolo-N"><small>Capitolo N</small>…</h2>`, chapters-plugin.ts),
 * scene breaks (`***` → «⁂»), the chat and log blocks.
 *
 * `id="testo"` and `tabindex="-1"` let the «Riprendi» link move the focus
 * here after scrolling back to the reader's place; `data-prose` is how the
 * reading-progress controller finds the text to measure.
 *
 * @example <Prose><Content /></Prose>
 */
---

<article id="testo" tabindex="-1" data-prose class="ct-prosa">
  <slot />
</article>
